  { key: 'issue-42', issue: 42, task: COMMON + '\n\nISSUE 42 — feat(attn): wire MLA + KDA HIP kernels into vLLM for K3 (gfx942). Prior state: the MLA half is validated end-to-end on beverin (job 600691, dummy weights); the actual VkernelMLA/VkernelKDA wiring lives in the cookbook sitecustomize.py + the private vLLM fork (EXTERNAL — do not modify); the on-cluster acceptance is tracked in issue #45. PR #46 landed capture-safe vLLM MoE integration in this repo.\nYour scope: audit what THIS repo provides for the KDA/MLA serving halves and whether anything in-repo blocks #45: vk_kda_delta_rule_fwd / vk_mla_fwd C ABI contracts (src/c/vkernels/capi/), CPU oracles for the serving validators, stream/capture safety of those entry points, and whether the #45 acceptance needs any in-repo helper that does not exist yet (e.g. a libvkernels host-build target for the cluster, documented in-repo). Close genuine in-repo gaps with a PR (tests/build/docs); if nothing in-repo is missing, deliver a precise findings report (what the cookbook side must do for KDA, referencing the exact C ABI signatures from capi headers) and post nothing — report back instead of opening an empty PR.' },
  { key: 'issue-45', issue: 45, task: COMMON + '\n\nISSUE 45 — validate(attn): on-cluster acceptance for VKERNELS MLA + KDA on K3/gfx942. Prior state: acceptance needs beverin MI300A + the private fork (cannot run here); an acceptance campaign is underway (baseline arm job 638514, evidence in meta/benchmarks/artifacts/k3-attn-accept/); the confounder (VkernelFusedExperts degenerate output) was root-caused and fixed via #74/#120, and PR #104\'s serve (job 640737) passed with the fix installed. The 5 acceptance items: (1) 6/6 factual probes with VKERNELS MLA+KDA, (2) KDA active + CPU-oracle cross-check max_rel<1e-2 + KDA_RECALL_PROBE passes with KDA on and fails on the all-MLA baseline, (3) rocprof shows zero AITER/Triton attention kernels, (4) no per-request latency regression <=1.05x at C=1 vs the K3_DISABLE_KDA=1 baseline, (5) AC4: flip defaults in the sbatch recipe after 1-4.\nYour scope: make the next beverin run mechanically executable — build/refresh the in-repo acceptance harness under meta/: a single runbook script (or small set) that executes each acceptance item and writes machine-readable evidence, including: the KDA_RECALL_PROBE runner, a rocprof post-processing check that asserts zero AITER/Triton attention kernel launches, the benchmark baseline comparator for item 4, and the gen_correctness inspection that distinguishes coherent text from smoke-only pass (the smoke matcher now records smoke:true/false — verify and use it). Update meta/benchmarks/artifacts/k3-attn-accept/README.md with the exact runbook. NO acceptance claims — tooling only. PR ready if locally verified to the extent possible.' },
];

const runs = await runs.all(tasks.map(t => ({ key: t.key, agent: 'worker', task: t.task })));

return tasks.map((t, i) => {
  const r = runs[i];
  return {
    issue: t.issue,
    key: t.key,
    completed: !!r,
    output: r ? String(r.output || '').slice(0, 6000) : 'NO RESULT',
  };
});

